==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
<!--Thanks Webster's.  One of these is Old French, the other Old Frisian.  Which is which?-->
OF. ''[[estanson]], [[estançon]]'', {{F.}} ''[[étançon]]'', from OF. ''[[estance]]'' a stay, a prop, from {{L.}} ''[[stans]], [[stantis]]'', standing, present participle of ''[[stare]]'' to stand.

===Pronunciation===
*{{enPR|stănʹshən}}, {{IPA|/ˈstænʃən/}}, {{SAMPA|/"st{nS@n/}} ''or'' 
*{{enPR|stänʹshən}}, {{IPA|/ˈstɑːnʃən/}}, {{SAMPA|/"stA:nS@n/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[vertical]] [[pole]], [[post]], or [[support]].
# A [[framework]] of such posts, used to [[secure]] or [[confine]] [[cattle]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[erect]] stanchions, or [[equip]] something with stanchions.
# To [[confine]] by means of stanchions, typically used for [[cattle]].

